# Fixed defect 580, 2026-10-10 (panel 207 R3; the sitting's `p207/loop`): a
# constant whose overflow comes on a loop's third turn. The walk over a
# constant's body reads a loop's condition and body once, so a cell the loop
# writes holds no value there (`check/const_writes.hero`), and `v @ v + 100`
# is not judged; spec § 4 refuses an integer operator at least where its
# operands are known, and this one's are not. It aborts where `V` is read, as
# overflow aborts at every width (spec § 7), the `1` before it flushed first.

constant V: u8
    v: u8 @ 0
    i: i64 @ 0

    while i < 3
        v @ v + 100
        i @ i + 1

    v

function main()
    print(1)
    print(V)
